                "entry_id": "d99aee02-9cfa-301b-b065-ef95911e13d7",
                "word": "chrysolite",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "368b9cee-f733-4d48-8e38-050b987dc3b1",
                        "entry_id": "d99aee02-9cfa-301b-b065-ef95911e13d7",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "chrysolites"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5942032f-0d09-3f96-920b-c619e15c7e0c",
                        "entry_id": "d99aee02-9cfa-301b-b065-ef95911e13d7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Originally, any of various green-coloured gems; later specifically peridot."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c142a448-5829-4509-99eb-2c3c243f0169",
                                "sense_id": "5942032f-0d09-3f96-920b-c619e15c7e0c",
                                "text": "Fran. Rueus[…]say as much of the chrysolite, a friend of wisdome, an enemy to folly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e7bd390-16f8-49aa-ade5-59d103080ca3",
                                "sense_id": "5942032f-0d09-3f96-920b-c619e15c7e0c",
                                "text": "And before he died, Taran-Ish had scrawled upon the altar of chrysolite with coarse shaky strokes the sign of DOOM."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa90ed35-d609-4bd4-9795-613435e82bfa",
                                "sense_id": "5942032f-0d09-3f96-920b-c619e15c7e0c",
                                "text": "A piece of marigold or bay leaf was imbedded in the metal, and over it a carbuncle or chrysolite was placed."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "eb69032e-2bf2-437b-91b4-6b401b08d2fd",
                        "source_entry_id": "d99aee02-9cfa-301b-b065-ef95911e13d7",
                        "source_sense_id": "5942032f-0d09-3f96-920b-c619e15c7e0c",
                        "source_sense_description": "a gemstone",
                        "target_lang_word": "chrysolithe",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chrysolithe",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa4c355c-3b07-3d4c-86c0-03a9d4e3c31e",
                                        "entry_id": "75a6f680-286d-3962-9316-e718618b1365",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Variante de chrysolite."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b7ad513-7b51-4d51-897f-157551ea5d08",
                                                "sense_id": "fa4c355c-3b07-3d4c-86c0-03a9d4e3c31e",
                                                "text": "Afin d’en finir avec cette orfèvrerie symbolique, disons encore que […] la sarde évoque les Séraphins, la topaze les Chérubins, le jaspe les Trônes, la chrysolithe les Dominations, le saphir les Vertus, l’onyx les Puissances, le béryl les Principautés, le rubis les Archanges et l’émeraude les Anges."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2589e567-7083-4e92-900d-6ee56c16cc29",
                                                "sense_id": "fa4c355c-3b07-3d4c-86c0-03a9d4e3c31e",
                                                "text": "La campagne s'étendait au loin, sous le soleil, dans une vapeur lumineuse. Des champs de maïs d'un vert clair de chrysolithe alternaient avec des cultures de millet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "abf3e918-6914-472d-93b0-f6d733d774d3",
                                                "sense_id": "fa4c355c-3b07-3d4c-86c0-03a9d4e3c31e",
                                                "text": "Il me faut parler de la chrysolithe tant que je m’en souviens, car la chrysolithe a été naturellement distinguée comme pierre largement supérieure aux autres, et que chacun devrait aimer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
